# Content rules

Use approved homepage copy from `docs/04-homepage-spec-and-copy.md`.

Do not replace business language with developer jargon.

Do not write:
- "innovative cutting-edge solutions" boilerplate
- fake social proof
- fake project outcomes
- fake statistics
- fake testimonials
- generic filler that sounds like a template

When a client case study lacks measurable numbers, use factual qualitative outcomes only.

SEO:
- one clear intent per page
- human-readable lowercase URLs
- unique metadata
- one logical H1
- semantic heading hierarchy
- canonical URLs
- XML sitemap
- Organization structured data from verified company facts only
- internal linking between Insights, Solutions, Work, and Academy
- no keyword stuffing
- no thin SEO pages

CMS:
- projects/case studies
- Insights
- Academy programs
- team
- testimonials
- selected statistics
- site settings

Do not make every sentence CMS-managed.
